course: dictionary
lesson: 1268
title: Animals in the dark
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words name one special animal, and the sentences around them give clues to what they mean. «Bushbabies are small African primates that leap several metres in the dark.» Primates are animals like monkeys, and leaping in the dark tells you this animal is active at night.
explain: The sentence says bushbabies cannot move their eyes, so they turn their heads instead. That clue explains why their eyes are so big: they gather light. Read the whole sentence, then the clues fit together like a puzzle.
explain: Look at this list: «the aye-aye taps on wood and listens, bats click and hear echoes, the kiwi sniffs with nostrils at the tip of its beak, the bushbaby gathers light with huge eyes.» Each animal has its own clever way to find food in the dark, and the bushbaby's way is its eyes.
fact: A bushbaby is a small African animal with huge round eyes, big ears and a long tail.
fact: Bushbabies live in trees and come out at night, so they are nocturnal.
fact: A bushbaby is also called a galago.
fact: Bushbabies are primates, related to monkeys and lemurs, and they leap from branch to branch eating insects and gum.
fact: The name bushbaby comes from its cry, which sounds like a crying baby.
exercise: «Bushbabies are small African primates that leap several metres in the dark.» What is a primate? | An insect that glows in the dark | *An animal related to monkeys and lemurs | A tree that grows in Africa
exercise: «Bushbabies are small African primates that leap several metres in the dark.» Find and copy one word that means jump. | small | dark | metres | *leap
exercise: Why is the bushbaby called a bushbaby? | It lives in a bush | *Its cry sounds like a crying baby | It is always very young | It sleeps in a cot
test: What does nocturnal mean? | Active in the morning | Asleep all year | *Active at night | Active only in the rain
test: «The bushbaby gathers light with huge eyes.» How does a bushbaby see well in the dark? | By swimming in rivers | By singing loudly | *With huge eyes that gather light | By wearing a torch
exam: Which animal is a bushbaby also called? | *A galago | A bat | A kiwi | An aye-aye
